WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.990 align:start position:0%
 
the movie is set around a family of  three curtis samantha and their mute  daughter hannah living in lagrange ohio  curtis works at a mining site and is  saving money for hannah's cochlear  implant surgery everything is going well  for the family until one day curtis sees  massive clouds forming in the sky from  his backyard within only seconds a  tornado manifests and starts approaching  the house when it starts to drizzle  curtis discovers the liquid falling from  the sky is not water but motor oil  before he can react his usually calm dog  turns aggressive and attacks him curtis  suddenly jolts up from his bed realizing  that all that was just a nightmare even  though it was strangely vivid curtis  decides to dismiss it and go on about  his day at breakfast he feels  uncomfortable letting hannah play with  the dog he takes her away and asks his  wife to put the dog outside the house  when he is not home samantha inquires  why but gets no reply as curtis sets off  to work dewort is curtis's work buddy  and a close friend like curtis dewort is  in need of money for his family so the  two get along pretty well that day at  work they are asked to take fewer breaks  since they took a leave because of a  storm last week the workers are stressed  because of the frequent storms which  curtis deduces is the cause of the  nightmare after work he goes to his  daughter's school for a parent-teacher  meeting on the drive back home another  violent storm hits and causes chaos it  rains motor oil causing curtis to crash  into a tree with his scared daughter  when he wakes up the car is surrounded  by strangers who try to break in to  steal it they break the glass window and  kidnap his daughter in front of his eyes  curtis lets out a loud scream and wakes  up in his bed again it turns out to be  just another one of his realistic dreams  but curtis can no longer dismiss this as  something trivial samantha notices him  breathing heavily and inquires what is  wrong but curtis doesn't tell her  anything trying not to worry her he has  decided to deal with the problem on his  own not by seeking medical help but by  obsessively looking into what his dreams  show him for instance he makes a fence  in their backyard to confine the dog in  case it turns aggressive like it did in  his dreams it relieves him to some  extent but he knows the primary problem  is the storm while trying to find a safe  zone curtis comes across an old storm  shelter in his backyard it has remained  closed for quite some time but he finds  the key in a drawer and opens it the  place is dusty and little but if  renovated it will be the safest place to  be in if something like his dream occurs  in real life at night samantha tries to  talk to curtis about his strange  behavior and is especially mad because  their dog has been left outside however  curtis is glued to the tv too busy to  answer her questions the following  morning he wakes up because of heavy  rainfall upon walking to the living room  he sees hannah looking out the window  and a stranger looking back at her from  their backyard curtis hugs his daughter  as the stranger tries to open the door  when the storm gets worse the entire  house starts moving making curtis fear  for his and his daughter's life just  when he accepts the inevitable he jerks  up from his bed he turns out to be  dreaming for the third time and the  dream was so intense that he has wet  himself in his sleep samantha comes into  the room asking him if he is all right  but curtis is too embarrassed to let her  know what happened he shouts at her to  stay away giving rise to arguments and  tension in the relationship even after  everything that happened curtis doesn't  want to acknowledge that he might be  mentally ill instead of going to a  doctor he picks up a book about mental  health from the library on his way back  he also hoards a trolley full of canned  food to store in the storm shelter that  day samantha organizes a family brunch  and is annoyed when her husband is laid  curtis has also been missing church  service and lagging at his job because  of his obsession with the oil storm at  night samantha waits for him in bed for  hours before finally falling asleep all  this time curtis is busy organizing food  in the storm shelter he hasn't slept  well for the past week and is worried  about his health hence the next day he  finally goes to the doctor with his  concerns he doesn't go into depth about  the dreams and is given some pills to  help him sleep better at the same time  samantha is with her insurance agent who  reveals that their appeal for hannah's  cochlear implant has been approved she  will soon go through surgery and will be  able to hear samantha excitedly returns  home and tells curtis the couple is  overjoyed which establishes a sense of  normalcy in their life again the next  morning goes even better as curtis wakes  up feeling fresh he slept like a baby  thanks to the medicine just when things  start to look good curtis hears a loud  storm again he asks his work buddy to  ward if he hears the noise but the sky  is clear showing no sign of clouds this  time he is definitely not asleep but the  sound continues troubling him the  experience gets so overwhelming that  curtis ends up vomiting and returning  home he then goes to his mother's place  wanting to talk to her about her mental  problems it turns out that she was  diagnosed with paranoid schizophrenia  and he is worried he might have the same  problem the mother tells him all about  her experience and how unknown people  would whisper in her ear all night she  was treated in her 30s and is perfectly  fine right now which makes curtis  believe his condition will also go away  the next day he goes to the bank to take  out a huge loan to repair the storm  shelter the loan puts his daughter's  surgery at risk because the family's  financial condition is not very good but  curtis has set his priorities straight  he genuinely believes that the storm is  about to strike one day or the other and  the shelter will save his family when it  does in the next scene we see him  visiting a therapist to talk about his  problems she breaks through his shell  and makes him talk about the nightmares  for the first time curtis feels a lot  better after talking about his problems  but is annoyed that therapy doesn't  provide an immediate cure on his way  back home a thunderstorm strikes curtis  panics unable to tell if it is real or  if he is dreaming he looks at samantha  in the back seat and sees her sleeping  peacefully which confirms that he is  hallucinating once again the night ends  somehow and curtis continues renovating  the storm shelter dewort brings him  tools from work at his request putting  his own job at risk samantha on the  other hand is terribly worried and angry  at her husband she still doesn't know  about the loan he has taken out but his  obsession with the shelter is ruining  their family at night she forces him to  talk about what is going on curtis still  hides the nightmares from her but tells  her about the loan angering samantha  even more she doesn't tolerate secrets  when it comes to their daughter and is  furious at curtis for putting her  surgery at risk she even thinks of  divorcing him because of the matter  after she calms down a little they  decide to talk the next day curtis takes  double the usual dosage of the sleeping  pills hoping that it will help but as a  result he suffers a stroke late at night  samantha wakes up in distress to witness  her husband vomiting blood and moving  violently she tries calling the  ambulance as he asks her to stop when  help arrives he sends them away claiming  that he is feeling better samantha can  no longer pretend that everything is  fine with their family she demands he  tell her everything making curtis  finally come clean about his nightmares  and the sleeping pills he also reveals  that he had a dream about dwart hurting  him in the storm which triggered the  stroke earlier samantha sympathizes with  him and is ready to do anything to help  him get better the next day curtis asks  his boss to change his shift because he  doesn't want to work with dwart anymore  they make an arrangement that hurts  dewart's schedule and the time he  provides for his family curtis feels bad  about troubling a friend but his mind is  set on removing anything that might be a  threat when the storm arrives after  everything curtis still continues  getting the nightmares as they get  progressively worse one night he sees  his wife standing still in the kitchen  staring at him she seems to have gotten  wet in a storm and is planning to kill  him the next morning he moves when she  tries to touch him making his distrust  clear curtis no longer knows who he can  trust because of this he misses many  days at work prompting his boss to visit  him the man sees the storm shelter and  finds out he has been using equipment  from work supplied by dewart this is the  last straw before he fires curtis from  work this puts the family deep into debt  all because of curtis's obsession a  furious samantha slaps him in the face  and asks him to manage the funds at any  cost they also cancel their annual beach  trip to save money for the surgery in  the following scene the family goes to  church to clear their minds with friends  and family curtis happens to meet dwart  who has been fired from his job because  of curtis he has family and financial  problems of his own and seeing curtis in  a better condition boils his blood dwart  has spread a rumor that curtis is insane  and needs medical attention the tension  between the two causes a physical fight  curtis calls everyone idiots for not  preparing for the oil storm declaring  that only his family will survive it  after the chaos the family returns home  in distress late at night an emergency  alarm is heard that wakes everyone up  the day curtis was worried about has  finally come in the darkness of the  night they rush to the shelter and hide  inside when morning comes curtis hears  the thunder get louder samantha on the  other hand asks him to come back to his  senses and open the door he does is told  to prove her wrong but outside is a  clear day the storm that struck last  night was only a minor one and cleared  up by morning their neighbors are  clearing the little debris left by the  storm which makes curtis finally see  that he has let the paranoia get the  best of him he drowns in the regret of  almost destroying his family over a few  nightmares samantha though is ready to  forgive him and start anew she brings  him to a good psychiatrist where curtis  gets proper treatment for his condition  since the storm shelter is the result of  his obsession he is asked to move away  for a while or go on a vacation to clear  up his mind samantha also thinks it is a  good idea because the family has been  too tense for the past month she  reorganizes their annual trip to the  beach for a week or so in the next scene  we see curtis playing with hannah at the  beach he hasn't had any nightmares in a  long time and it is evident in his mood  as the two play hannah stops giggling  abruptly curtis looks at her and sees  her signing storm on turning around  curtis sees a storm double the size of  the ones he used to dream of it is  coming their way threatening to engulf  the entire city curtis cannot tell if it  is real but seeing samantha's face drop  he registers that she can see it too the  film ends as the family gets ready to  return home before they are caught in  the oil storm  subscribe for more videos like this turn  on notifications and leave a like to  help the channel out thank you for  watching

